-    "reason": "The induce path gains two things and neither is reachable from any code these artifacts execute. (1) `LocalGGUFProposer.generate()` adds `repeat_penalty`/`repeat_last_n` to the llama-server `/completion` payload, guarded by `if codeonly_eligible` -- so it is present ONLY on a live induce call and absent on every other call shape, refactor included. (2) A candidate that parses and defines the required functions is now dry-run/AST-checked via `arc_engine_static_validation.validate_engine_code`, and on a mechanical defect is re-asked once with a neutral block. Both are LIVE-GENERATION behaviours: they change what a running llama-server is asked for and whether its answer is accepted. Also added: a `n_induce_defect_reasks` counter and its `llm.induce_defect_reasks` witness key (a new key, never a changed one), and a new keyword-only `engine_transitions=None` argument whose default reproduces the old call exactly. The defect gate cannot turn a previously-successful call into a failure: it only ever spends one further attempt, and only while an attempt remains (`attempt < tries - 1`), which is pinned by `tests/python/test_arc_induce_repeat_penalty_and_reask_2026_07_31.py`.",
