-    "reason": "`plan_in_model`'s `termination_reason` gains a third value `depth_capped`, and `diagnostics` gains a `depth_truncated_nodes` count, so a search stopped by `max_depth` is no longer reported as `queue_exhausted` (\"I searched the reachable set exhaustively and there is no plan\") -- the same conflation fixed the same day in the goal gate this function is guarded by. Every code path RETURNS exactly what it returned before: the same plan, or the same None. Nothing in the tree branches on the string (the only readers are `scripts/arc_plan_in_model_nav_solve.py`, which formats it for display, and the `ttt_prior_engine_plan_diagnostics` blob the agent stores verbatim).",
-    "evidence": "DIFFERENTIAL EXECUTION, not a reading of the diff: the pre-change module is materialised from git HEAD into a separate namespace and both versions are run over 600 randomised (engine, goal, root, max_nodes, max_depth, goal_energy) cases spanning four engine mechanic families and both search loops. RETURN VALUES DIFFER IN 0 OF 600 (`results/arc_plan_in_model_depth_20260731/inertness_differential.json`). The same run's vacuity guard shows the corpus really does exercise the change -- 146 cases relabel `queue_exhausted -> depth_capped` -- while 111 cases keep `queue_exhausted` and 152 keep `max_nodes_reached`, so this is a split, not a blanket rename. Additionally pinned by `tests/python/test_arc_plan_in_model_depth_capped_2026_07_31.py` (9 tests, 6/6 real mutations killed with a deliberate inert control surviving, `results/arc_plan_in_model_depth_20260731/mutation_check.json`), and verified on the real origin cell: the tn36 engine + root fixture that the 2026-07-30 audit recorded now reports `depth_capped` at `max_depth=40` while still finding the identical 61-action plan at 80 (`results/arc_plan_in_model_depth_20260731/tn36_plan_termination.json`).",
