-    "reason": "The induce path gains two things and neither is reachable from any code these artifacts execute. (1) `LocalGGUFProposer.generate()` adds `repeat_penalty`/`repeat_last_n` to the llama-server `/completion` payload, guarded by `if codeonly_eligible` -- so it is present ONLY on a live induce call and absent on every other call shape, refactor included. (2) A candidate that parses and defines the required functions is now dry-run/AST-checked via `arc_engine_static_validation.validate_engine_code`, and on a mechanical defect is re-asked once with a neutral block. Both are LIVE-GENERATION behaviours: they change what a running llama-server is asked for and whether its answer is accepted. Also added: a `n_induce_defect_reasks` counter and its `llm.induce_defect_reasks` witness key (a new key, never a changed one), and a new keyword-only `engine_transitions=None` argument whose default reproduces the old call exactly. The defect gate cannot turn a previously-successful call into a failure: it only ever spends one further attempt, and only while an attempt remains (`attempt < tries - 1`), which is pinned by `tests/python/test_arc_induce_repeat_penalty_and_reask_2026_07_31.py`.",
-    "evidence": "DIFFERENTIAL EXECUTION AT THE ARTIFACT LEVEL, not a reading of the diff: this artifact was REBUILT under the changed module using its own recorded `rebuild_command` (canonical repo path, `CARNOT_ARC_E3_DIR` preserved), and the rebuild was deep-diffed leaf-by-leaf against the published version -- 1,313 leaves compared, 4 substantive fields moved. The four non-annotation fields that moved were `aggregation_wall_s` and three `code_provenance` fields (the declared dependency's mtime, its sha256, and the diff-stat-vs-HEAD string that quite properly now describes this very change). Every head-to-head statistic -- coverage 4/13 vs 12/13, meanB 0.062677 vs 0.384328, p_cov 0.007812, p_meanB 0.000977, N=13 -- is unchanged. The rebuild output is retained OUT of tree at `scratchpad/phase2/after/experiment_6021_inducer_head_to_head_qwen27b_vs_gemma31b.json`. The rebuild was then DISCARDED and the published artifact restored, because regenerating it drops annotations the generator does not emit: it wiped this artifact's `original_timings_superseded_by_rebuild` block and all 2 prior `freshness_acknowledgements`. That is the exact trap the block itself warns about -- 'When the only drift is timing, acknowledge rather than rebuild' -- recorded when commit 0da7f75ad overwrote these same measured timings. So the rebuild was used as PROOF of inertness and not as the artifact of record, which is strictly stronger evidence than an acknowledgement argued from the source diff.",
